# Step 20: Common Troubleshooting

| Issue                    | Solution                                                                                                   |
| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Jenkins won't start      | Check `sudo systemctl status jenkins` and inspect logs with `sudo journalctl -u jenkins`                   |
| Can't access port 8080   | Ensure the EC2 security group allows inbound TCP on port 8080 and the instance firewall permits it         |
| Git clone fails          | Verify repository URL and credentials (PAT or SSH key)                                                     |
| Docker permission denied | Add the `jenkins` user to the `docker` group and restart Jenkins                                           |
| Webhook not triggering   | Verify the webhook URL, ensure Jenkins is reachable from GitHub, and check webhook delivery logs in GitHub |

## Typical CI/CD Workflow

```text
Developer pushes code
        │
        ▼
GitHub Repository
        │
        ▼
Webhook triggers Jenkins
        │
        ▼
Checkout source
        │
        ▼
Run tests
        │
        ▼
Build application
        │
        ▼
Build Docker image (optional)
        │
        ▼
Deploy to EC2 / ECS / Kubernetes
        │
        ▼
Application updated
```

